# Aegis scan exclusions (gitignore-style).
#
# Only machine-generated files belong here. A finding in a generated
# file is a false positive that reappears whenever the generator's
# output shifts — the baseline keys on file:line:content-digest, so
# every regeneration invalidates the entry and the gate fails on
# noise instead of on a real leak.
#
# Note: keep this file's own prose free of the patterns it names —
# the scanner reads this file too, and a comment that quotes a rule
# name is itself a finding.

# Build artifacts. Contains gigabytes of compiled Rust / WASM — scanning
# them hangs aegis (>120s). CI runners have no pre-existing build
# directories so these exclusions only affect local development.
target/
# trunk build output — the compiled WASM bundle (13MB+) is a binary blob
# that causes aegis to hang.
web/dist/

# Release staging (xtask dist --web / --native) — the built WASM bundle
# and its manifest. Generated output, rebuilt per release; its bytes
# move with every build.
dist/

# fuzz workspace — 23GB of corpus inputs, crash artifacts, and build
# targets. aegis hangs on this volume. The fuzz workspace has its own
# CI gate and is a separate concern from the main codebase scan.
fuzz/

# Generated by `xtask changelog` from the commit log. Its line numbers
# move with every commit, and its text is commit subjects rather than
# authored prose.
docs/CHANGELOG.md

# Generated by `xtask scripts` — a report of the CS6 .jsf script run.
# Carries a generation timestamp, which trips a numeric PII rule.
corpus/scripts-report.json

# Claude Code session state — machine-generated lock files and task
# metadata written while the agent works. Their byte content (pids,
# timestamps, session uuids) trips the numeric PII rules and changes
# per session, so a baseline entry can never stick.
.claude/

# Scratch notes (uncommitted operator notes, screenshots). Untracked
# working files, not source; their content churns constantly.
temp/

# Throwaway probe helpers (headless browser drivers and their throwaway
# scripts). Git-ignored working files, not source; every run rewrites
# them, so their findings can never stick to the baseline.
.gitignore-scratch/

# Proprietary Adobe reference install (git-ignored working material,
# see CLAUDE.md source/ rules). Third-party binaries and vendor JS —
# every finding there is noise by definition, and the files churn.
source/

# Session log (git-ignored per AGENTS.md, appended to close every task).
# Its prose quotes CS6 resource command ids, which trip the numeric PII
# rules, and every session appends — line-keyed baseline entries can
# never stick.
log/

# The baseline file itself — machine-generated from a scan, and the
# findings it records (numeric literals, prose) land back in it. Every
# regeneration rewrites its content, so its own entries would be
# invalidated by the regeneration that produced them.
.aegis-baseline.json
